ior where explicitly documented; future effectiveness is not fabricated where the source provides no result.","outcome":"D52 establishes a repair knowledge model that separates immediate recovery from durable prevention.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED_WITH_INFERENCE_LABEL","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"MULTIPLE_OFFICIAL_AVAILABILITY_REPORTS","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Reports: May 2023, August 2024, September 2024, January 2025, February 2025","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2023-2025","evidence_type":"Official availability reports and incident analysis","source_ref":"github_successful_repairs_multi_incident_synthesis"},"related_records":["D52-B01-R01","D52-B02-R01","D52-B03-R01","D52-B04-R01","D52-B05-R01","D52-B06-R01","D52-B07-R01","D52-B08-R01","D52-B09-R01","D52-B10-R01"],"relationships":["derived_from","synthesizes","relates_to"]}

{"record_id":"D52-B11-R01","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B11","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"DNS infrastructure recovery","concept":"Diagnosis of cascading DNS failure after database migration","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"How was the October 2024 GitHub DNS incident diagnosed?","answer":"The incident was traced to DNS infrastructure failing to resolve lookups at one site following a database migration, with attempts to recover the database producing cascading failures that affected DNS systems at that site.","context":"GitHub October 11 2024 availability incident.","objective":"Identify the infrastructure dependency causing DNS resolution failure and restore service without extending the failure to healthy sites.","attempted_solution":"The team initially attempted to repoint the degraded DNS site to a different site.","failure":"The repointing restored connectivity within the degraded site but introduced connectivity problems from healthy sites back to the degraded site.","evidence":"GitHub reported that DNS resolution failures followed a database migration and that the first remediation attempt created additional connectivity problems.","cause":"Database migration and subsequent database recovery problems caused cascading DNS infrastructure failures.","root_cause":"Failure of DNS infrastructure recovery following database migration, combined with an ineffective initial cross-site repointing strategy.","impact":"Copilot, Actions, and code search experienced degradation; code search requests failed during a prolonged window.","containment":"The team abandoned the ineffective repointing approach and developed a different remediation plan.","remediation":"Temporary DNS resolution capabilities were deployed directly to the degraded site.","lessons":"Repair diagnosis must account for dependency direction and avoid assuming that redirecting traffic to another site is safe when cross-site connectivity is itself affected.","validation_status":"VALIDATED_AGAINST_OFFICIAL_POSTMORTEM","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"OFFICIAL_POSTMORTEM","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: October 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2024-11-14","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"turn2search12"},"related_records":["D51"],"relationships":["related_to","contrasts_with"]}

{"record_id":"D52-B11-R02","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B11","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"DNS infrastructure recovery","concept":"Temporary DNS resolution deployment","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"What immediate repair restored DNS resolution during the October 2024 GitHub incident?","answer":"GitHub deployed temporary DNS resolution capabilities to the degraded site as the next mitigation phase after the earlier site-repointing approach proved unsuitable.","context":"October 11 2024 DNS infrastructure incident.","objective":"Restore DNS resolution at the degraded site while avoiding additional cross-site connectivity problems.","attempted_solution":"Deploy temporary DNS resolution capabilities directly at the affected site.","failure":"No failure of the documented final mitigation was reported; DNS recovery began after deployment.","evidence":"DNS resolution began recovering at 21:46 UTC after the remediation phase started and was fully healthy at 22:16 UTC.","cause":"The degraded site lacked functioning DNS resolution after cascading infrastructure failures.","root_cause":"The DNS dependency required local recovery rather than the earlier cross-site redirection strategy.","impact":"DNS-dependent GitHub functionality had been degraded.","containment":"Temporary DNS capability was deployed locally at the affected site.","remediation":"Restore the original infrastructure after public service recovery and harden resilience and automation.","lessons":"When a dependency is locally impaired, a temporary local capability can provide a controlled recovery path while the underlying infrastructure is repaired.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: October 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2024-11-14","evidence_type":"Official availability re