{"record_id":"D52-B13-R01","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B13","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Web service overload recovery","concept":"Diagnosis of cascading load amplification","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"What caused the December 2024 GitHub web service overload?","answer":"Planned maintenance unintentionally caused the live updates service to fail. Clients then refreshed aggressively because automatic updates were unavailable, increasing load on web servers and causing broad errors and timeouts.","context":"GitHub December 17 2024 incident.","objective":"Identify the mechanism by which a dependency failure amplified web-server load.","attempted_solution":"Restore the failed live updates service and reduce resulting traffic pressure.","failure":"The live updates failure caused clients to refresh aggressively, increasing load beyond the original failure.","evidence":"GitHub explicitly described the live updates failure, aggressive client refresh behavior, and resulting web-server overload.","cause":"Live updates service failure during planned maintenance.","root_cause":"Failure of a service dependency created client-side retry/refresh amplification.","impact":"Users experienced intermittent errors and timeouts across multiple GitHub services.","containment":"Rollback of maintenance changes and service scaling were used.","remediation":"Improve monitoring higher in the request path and alerting coverage.","lessons":"Repair diagnosis should include feedback loops created by clients when a dependency becomes unavailable.","validation_status":"VALIDATED_AGAINST_OFFICIAL_POSTMORTEM","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"OFFICIAL_POSTMORTEM","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: December 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2025-01-15","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"turn2search2"},"related_records":["D51"],"relationships":["related_to"]}

{"record_id":"D52-B13-R02","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B13","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Web service recovery","concept":"Rollback and capacity scaling","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"What immediate repair restored GitHub web service capacity in December 2024?","answer":"GitHub rolled back the planned-maintenance changes and scaled the affected service to handle the increased traffic from WebSocket clients.","context":"December 17 2024 web-service overload incident.","objective":"Remove the triggering change and provide enough capacity to absorb the resulting request surge.","attempted_solution":"Rollback the maintenance changes and increase service capacity.","failure":"No failure of the final mitigation was reported.","evidence":"GitHub stated that the incident was mitigated through rollback and scaling.","cause":"Live updates failure caused aggressive client refresh behavior.","root_cause":"Maintenance change caused a dependency outage that amplified client traffic.","impact":"Broad web-service errors and timeouts occurred.","containment":"Rollback removed the triggering maintenance changes.","remediation":"Scale capacity and improve upstream monitoring.","lessons":"When recovery includes both a trigger removal and traffic amplification, rollback and capacity restoration may need to occur together.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: December 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2025-01-15","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"turn2search2"},"related_records":["D52-B13-R01"],"relationships":["fixes","derived_from"]}

{"record_id":"D52-B13-R03","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B13","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Recovery verification","concept":"Post-rollback service stabilization","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"How was the December 2024 GitHub web-service repair verified?","answer":"The incident was mitigated after the maintenance changes were rolled back and capacity was increased. GitHub subsequently identified the broad impact and planned additional monitoring and alerting improvements.","context":"December 17 2024 GitHub availability incident.","objective":"Confirm that rollback and scaling removed the active overload condition.","attempted_solution":"Observe service behavior after rollback and scaling.","failure":"The incident revealed that existing alerting had gaps in correctly identifying impact while servers were overloaded.","evidence":"GitHub reported that mitigation occurred through rollback and scaling, while impact assessment improved after mitigation.","cause":"Live updates failure and resulting request amplification.","root_cause":"Maintenance-induced dependency failure combined with client refresh behavior.","impact":"8.5% average error rate, peaking at 44.3%, with broad feature impact.","containment":"Rollback and scaling.","remediation":"Monitoring higher in the request path and improved alerting.","lessons":"Verification should distinguish service restoration from complete understanding of incident scope.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: December 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2025-01-15","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"turn2search2"},"related_records":["D52-B13-R02"],"relationships":["verifies","learned_from"]}

{"record_id":"D52-B13-R04","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B13","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Observability remediation","concept":"Higher-path monitoring","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"What durable observability repair followed the December 2024 overload?","answer":"GitHub added monitoring higher in the request path to capture this type of failure and worked to improve alerting so the scope of impact could be detected more accurately.","context":"Post-incident remediation for the December 2024 web overload.","objective":"Detect upstream dependency failures and broadening impact earlier.","attempted_solution":"Add higher-path monitoring and improve alerting.","failure":"Existing alerting had gaps because overloaded web servers affected the ability to assess service impact correctly.","evidence":"GitHub explicitly stated that it added monitoring higher in the request path and was improving alerting.","cause":"Failure occurred upstream but manifested as downstream web-server overload.","root_cause":"Insufficient observability of the request path and impact scope.","impact":"Delayed understanding of the full service impact.","containment":"Rollback and scaling restored service.","remediation":"Higher-path monitoring and improved alerting.","lessons":"Observability should cover the dependency path leading to an outage, not only the final overloaded component.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: December 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2025-01-15","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"turn2search2"},"related_records":["D52-B13-R03"],"relationships":["remediates","learned_from"]}

{"record_id":"D52-B13-R05","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B13","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Feedback-loop repair","concept":"Client retry amplification awareness","knowledge_type":"INFERENCE","question":"What repair principle can be derived from the December 2024 overload?","answer":"A repair system should model client retry, refresh, or reconnect behavior because restoring a failed dependency without controlling the resulting traffic amplification can leave the service overloaded.","context":"Inference derived from GitHub's documented live-updates failure and aggressive client refresh behavior.","objective":"Improve diagnosis and repair of distributed systems with reactive clients.","attempted_solution":"Treat the dependency failure as an isolated component problem.","failure":"Client behavior amplified the original failure into a broader overload.","evidence":"GitHub reported that clients refreshed aggressively when live updates were unavailable.","cause":"Dependency failure triggered client-side refresh amplification.","root_cause":"The system lacked sufficient isolation between dependency failure and client traffic behavior.","impact":"Web-server overload and broad errors.","containment":"Rollback and scaling.","remediation":"Monitor request-path effects and account for retry amplification in recovery design.","lessons":"Successful repair must account for system feedback loops, not just component state.","validation_status":"VALIDATED_AGAINST_OFFICIAL_POSTMORTEM","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"OFFICIAL_POSTMORTEM","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub Availability Report: December 2024","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2025-01-15","evidence_type":"Official postmortem plus derived engineering inference","source_ref":"turn2search2"},"related_records":["D52-B13-R01","D52-B13-R04"],"relationships":["derived_from","constrains"]}

