{"record_id":"D52-B35-R03","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B35","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Second failure verification","concept":"Handling residual cache-write sources","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"Why was a second repair required during the February 9 incident?","answer":"A second source of cache updates continued producing high-volume synchronous writes. GitHub disabled that source and restarted the Git proxy again after replication delays caused another connection-exhaustion cascade.","context":"Second February 9 2026 degradation period.","objective":"Remove a residual write source that was not covered by the first mitigation.","attempted_solution":"Disable only asynchronous cache rewrites.","failure":"Another cache-update source continued generating synchronous writes.","evidence":"GitHub explicitly states that the second incident required disabling an additional source of cache rewrites and restarting the proxy.","cause":"Synchronous cache-write amplification.","root_cause":"The initial mitigation did not cover all cache-update paths.","impact":"Replication delays and another Git HTTPS proxy connection-exhaustion cascade.","containment":"Disable the remaining cache-update source and restart the proxy.","remediation":"Identify and control all write sources and improve rollback behavior.","lessons":"Containment must cover the complete causal mechanism, including alternative or previously overlooked write paths.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub availability report: February 2026","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2026-03-11","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"GITHUB_AVAILABILITY_FEBRUARY_2026"},"related_records":["D52-B35-R02"],"relationships":["related_to","fixes"]}
