{"record_id":"D52-B60-R01","dataset_id":"D52","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B60","topic":"Successful Repairs","subtopic":"Load-balancer overload recovery","concept":"Retry-amplification containment","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","question":"How was the August 17 2026 GitHub front-door outage diagnosed?","answer":"The incident was traced to a traffic peak that pushed a datacenter's load balancers beyond their limits. A service-mesh sidecar reached its concurrency limit without scaling, network flow limits were exhausted, and a latent client retry bug amplified authentication traffic.","context":"Issues, pull requests, APIs, Actions, Copilot, authentication, and webhooks were affected through shared load-balancing infrastructure.","objective":"Identify the overload chain and the feedback mechanism preventing recovery.","attempted_solution":"Trace traffic saturation, service-mesh limits, network flow exhaustion, and retry amplification.","failure":"Retry traffic increased pressure on an already saturated authentication path.","evidence":"GitHub documented the load-balancer, sidecar, network-flow, and client-retry failure chain.","cause":"Load-balancer and service-mesh capacity exhaustion amplified by retries.","root_cause":"Insufficient scaling of the service-mesh sidecar combined with retry behavior that amplified partial degradation.","impact":"Broad multi-service front-door failures and latency.","containment":"Shift traffic, reduce gateway retries, stop saturated load-balancer processes, block retry-triggering requests, and ramp traffic gradually.","remediation":"Correct autoscaling policies, audit concurrency/scaling limits, review retry/backoff limits, fix retry behavior, improve capacity monitoring and regional failover safeguards.","lessons":"Retries can convert partial dependency degradation into a broader overload and must be treated as part of the failure system.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":{"source_title":"GitHub availability report: August 2026","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2026-09-09","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"GITHUB_AVAILABILITY_AUGUST_2026"},"related_records":["D51"],"relationships":["causes","related_to"]}

