{"record_id":"D53-B31-R01","dataset_id":"D53","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B31","topic":"Failed Repairs","subtopic":"Deployment Capacity","concept":"Rollback did not immediately repair capacity exhaustion","knowledge_type":"EXPERIENCE","question":"Why was rolling back the August 6 deployment insufficient as an immediate repair?","answer":"The deployment contents were not the root cause. Rolling back confirmed that, but the rollout had already reduced running capacity at one site while the remaining sites were pushed beyond their limits. Capacity exhaustion therefore persisted after rollback until additional capacity was expanded.","context":"GitHub Actions incident on August 6, 2026.","objective":"Capture why reversing the triggering deployment did not itself restore service.","attempted_solution":"Roll back the routine deployment.","failure":"Rollback did not immediately restore sufficient serving capacity.","evidence":"GitHub states that the deployment was rolled back to confirm its contents were not at fault, while the affected services remained capacity constrained.","cause":"Temporary capacity reduction during rollout combined with insufficient headroom.","root_cause":"The system was operating close to capacity and lacked enough headroom to tolerate the rollout-induced capacity reduction.","impact":"Actions workflows failed, remained queued, or started late.","containment":"Expand capacity for saturated services and throttle incoming webhook-triggered work.","remediation":"Increase service and ingress headroom, enable autoscaling, and avoid capacity reductions during deployment.","lessons":"A rollback can remove a triggering change without reversing resource exhaustion already created by the rollout.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":[{"source_title":"GitHub availability report: August 2026","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2026-09-09","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"GITHUB_AVAILABILITY_AUGUST_2026"}],"related_records":["D53-B31-R02"],"relationships":{"causes":[],"fixes":[],"related_to":["D53-B31-R02"],"learned_from":["D53-B31-R01"]}}

{"record_id":"D53-B31-R02","dataset_id":"D53","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B31","topic":"Failed Repairs","subtopic":"Deployment Capacity","concept":"Capacity restoration was required after rollback","knowledge_type":"EXPERIENCE","question":"What repair was required after rollback failed to restore enough capacity?","answer":"The response required expanding capacity for saturated services and throttling incoming webhook-triggered work so the system could stabilize. Rollback alone was therefore rejected as an adequate recovery action.","context":"August 6, 2026 GitHub Actions incident.","objective":"Identify the additional repair required after rollback.","attempted_solution":"Rely on deployment rollback as the primary restoration action.","failure":"The service remained capacity constrained because rollback did not restore the missing headroom.","evidence":"The official report states that capacity was expanded over roughly the next two hours while incoming webhook-triggered work was throttled.","cause":"Insufficient spare capacity across remaining sites.","root_cause":"Deployment safety depended on capacity headroom that was not actually available under the existing load.","impact":"Continued workflow failures and queue growth.","containment":"Expand capacity and throttle incoming work.","remediation":"Add headroom and autoscaling and make rollout procedures avoid capacity reductions.","lessons":"Recovery plans must address current resource state, not only revert the configuration change that preceded the failure.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":[{"source_title":"GitHub availability report: August 2026","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2026-09-09","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"GITHUB_AVAILABILITY_AUGUST_2026"}],"related_records":["D53-B31-R01"],"relationships":{"causes":[],"fixes":[],"relate