{"record_id":"D53-B40-R04","dataset_id":"D53","dataset_version":"1.0.0","schema_version":"1.0.0","batch":"B40","topic":"Failed Repairs","subtopic":"Database Throttling","concept":"Database protection required both demand control and workload optimization","knowledge_type":"EXPERIENCE","question":"What combination of durable repairs followed the August 26 incident?","answer":"The documented follow-up combined query optimization, automatic circuit breaking, protections against harmful primary fallback, stuck-run cleanup, and broader scaling/resiliency work.","context":"August 26, 2026 GitHub Actions incident.","objective":"Capture the multi-layer remediation required after partial incident fixes.","attempted_solution":"Treat failover and manual throttling as sufficient.","failure":"The incident revealed several independent recovery and capacity weaknesses.","evidence":"GitHub lists multiple follow-up actions spanning code efficiency, circuit breaking, database fallback, stuck jobs, scaling and resiliency.","cause":"Shared database pressure interacted with multiple dependent systems.","root_cause":"No single repair addressed the entire overload and recovery chain.","impact":"Repeated risk across database, job assignment and queued-work paths.","containment":"Manual throttling and recovery changes.","remediation":"Apply layered workload, database, queue and automation improvements.","lessons":"Complex operational failures often require a chain of complementary repairs rather than one root fix.","validation_status":"SOURCE_VALIDATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_SOURCE","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":[{"source_title":"GitHub availability report: August 2026","publisher":"GitHub","publication_date":"2026-09-09","evidence_type":"Official availability report","source_ref":"GITHUB_AVAILABILITY_AUGUST_2026"}],"related_records":["D53-B40-R01","D53-B40-R03","D53-B40-R05"],"relationships":{"fixes":["D53-B40-R01"],"composes_with":["D53-B40-R03","D